/env.json
# No trailing slash: in a git worktree this is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's
# node_modules (see worktree.symlinkDirectories), and `/node_modules/` matches a
# directory only — leaving the symlink untracked and one `git add -A` away from
# committing an absolute path off this machine.
/node_modules
/.homeybuild/
/dev/csv/
# Throwaway harness for eyeballing the pair/repair views in a browser.
/dev/preview/

# Personal Homey data — flow/device/zone exports pulled off the live hub with
# `homey api raw`. These carry the home's real device ids, user names and push
# targets, and are nobody else's business. Dumps belong in a scratchpad outside
# the repo; these patterns are a backstop for when one lands in it anyway.
backup_all_advancedflows*.json
advancedflow*.json
*.homeyflows.json
/homey-dump/